<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         THE "FIRE" DESIGN LAYER — the tokens the four shared CUSTOM-DRAWN
         controls need, that the base ladder in `FireTokens.axaml` does not
         carry.

         Its own file rather than an addition to `FireTokens.axaml` for one
         concrete reason: the two are authored concurrently, and two blocks
         appended to one `<Styles.Resources>` merge cleanly in git while
         producing a DUPLICATE `x:Key` — which builds clean and then crashes
         the whole app at `App.Initialize()`. Merged dictionaries resolve
         last-wins instead, so a second file cannot do that.

         What is here, and nothing else:

         1. THE EIGHT GEAR-CATEGORY IDENTITY COLOURS. Section 01 of the
            owner's Implementation Spec ("GEAR CATEGORY IDENTITY · USED IN THE
            RIG, GEAR LIST AND TONE CHIPS") lists them as FIXED, DO NOT
            REASSIGN — the same standing the six string colours have. They are
            the arc colour of a `FireKnob`, and they are reached through
            `FireUnitState.Category`, never as a brush a caller picks: a knob
            that took a `Color` could be given the wrong identity.
            `DotCharter.Tests/UI/FireUnitIdentityTests` pins every one of the
            eight values against the spec and fails if a hue is reassigned.

         2. THE KNOB DIAL. `radial-gradient(circle at 34% 26%, #2f3236,
            #15181d 70%)` + a 1px rgba(255,255,255,.14) rim, straight out of
            `Amp and FX Rig.dc.html`. It lives here rather than in the control
            so the recipe is in the dictionary with every other colour, and so
            the control carries no literal hex at all.

         SIZES ARE NOT TOKENS HERE. A custom-drawn control's geometry is code
         (`FireKnobGeometry`, `FireLevelScale`, `FireProgressGeometry`) — the
         same call `KnobMath` already made for the pedalboard. Only colour goes
         through the dictionary.

         The controls: `DotCharter.UI/Controls/Fire/`.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <Styles.Resources>

        <!-- ─── Gear-category identity · FIXED, DO NOT REASSIGN ─────────────── -->
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitDynamics" Color="#8FA3BD" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitAmps" Color="#F0A54A" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitCabinets" Color="#C98F5E" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitDrive" Color="#E05A5A" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitEq" Color="#4ADE80" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitModulation" Color="#E879B9" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitDelay" Color="#3EC9C0" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireUnitUtility" Color="#A78BFA" />

        <!-- ─── The knob dial ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
        <RadialGradientBrush x:Key="FireDialFill"
                             Center="34%,26%" GradientOrigin="34%,26%"
                             RadiusX="70%" RadiusY="70%">
            <GradientStop Offset="0" Color="#2F3236" />
            <GradientStop Offset="1" Color="#15181D" />
        </RadialGradientBrush>
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireDialRim" Color="#24FFFFFF" />       <!-- rgba(255,255,255,.14) -->
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FireDialRimHover" Color="#3DFFFFFF" />  <!-- .24 — the hover state -->

    </Styles.Resources>
</Styles>
